  "verbalization": "Cefoperazone, a broad-spectrum antibiotic, is shown to bind to Slc22a7 and Slc22a11, both of which are involved in the transport of organic anions across cellular membranes. These transporters are further linked to Slc22a8, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Cefoperazone may influence the cellular uptake or efflux of organic anions. The binding of Cefoperazone to Slc22a7 and Slc22a11, which are part of the same functional pathway, implies that the drug may interfere with the transport of anionic compounds, potentially altering their distribution within the cell. This mechanism is supported by the presence of multiple paths with high confidence scores, indicating a consistent and plausible interaction between Cefoperazone and Slc22a8. The evidence suggests that Cefoperazone may act through a transport-related pathway, affecting the movement of organic anions, which could have implications for drug metabolism and toxicity.",
